Welcome to CSI^ho.

Before compiling, check if you have at least
 - ocaml 3.12
 - camlidl 1.05

The following programs and libraries may already be available on your machine:
 - gcc-c++ (provides g++)
 - zlib-devel
 - glibc-static 2.12-1(if you compile static)
 - libxslt-devel
 - libxml-devel
 - pkg-config

To compile, type

 $ make

To run the tool, type

 $ ./csiho

To run the tool in its automatic mode, use one of

 $ ./csiho.sh <file>
 $ ./csiho -C HOCR -s AUTO -c ho.conf <file>

To generate (html) documentation, type

 $ make doc

After successful compilation you can type

 $ make clean

to clean up compiled sources.

See mk/README for a list of other available targets.

Information about the implementation of CSI can be found in

 $ doc/index.html

Never forget that you can also ask CSI itself, e.g.,

 $ ./csiho --help

shows a list of options and explains the strategy language,

 $ ./csiho --processors

gives a comprehensive list of (non)confluence processors.
Furthermore most processors can explain their flags, e.g.,

 $ ./csiho -s 'hocr --help' <trs>

prints the flags one can specify for the Church-Rosser transformation
processor (for internal reasons a TRS must be specified).

NOTE: CSI^ho is an extension of CSI and ttt2, which are essentially the same
tool, so if you build CSI^ho you will also get a csi and a ttt2 executable.